          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em equivariant Pontrjagin theorem
            should generalize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
            from plain
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cobordism+theory"} equivariant cobordism theory
          %p
            Where the plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
            identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifolds"} normally framed submanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Cohomotopy"} equivariant Cohomotopy
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+locus"} fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifold"} normal framing
            inherits the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representation"} linear representation
            of the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-degree"} RO(G)-degree
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A fully general version of an equivariant Pontrjagin theorem is not known (?) and not expected to exist (?) because
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+transversality+theorem"} Thom's transversality theorem
            (which, in one formulation or another, underlies the proof of the ordinary
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+functions"} equivariant functions
            need to send
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
            of fixed points to an isolated fixed point has no equivariant deformation whatsoever, let along a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+point"} regular
            one.
          %h3#for_free_manifolds
            For free
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This problem with transversaliuty goes away when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifold"} G-manifold
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Cruickshank99"} Cruickshank 99, Thm. 5.06
          %p
            Of course, this case is only “mildly equivariant”: When the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifold"} G-manifold
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
            then its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            should essentially reduce to plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            %a{:href => "#Cruickshank99"} Cruickshank 99, Cor. 6.0.13
            identifies, in this case,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Cohomotopy"} equivariant Cohomotopy
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+twisted-framed+submanifolds"} normally twisted-framed submanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Pontrjagin+theorem"} twisted Pontrjagin theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cruickshank03"}> Cruickshank 03, Lemma 5.2
            ) on the quotient.
