          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesPontrjaginThomConstruction Pontrjagin-Thom construction
            %h4#ReferencesPontrjaginConstruction Pontrjagin’s construction
            %h5#general General
            %p
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+theorem"} Pontryagin theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifold"} framed
              version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+construction"} Pontrjagin-Thom construction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifolds"} normally framed submanifolds
              with their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+charge"} Cohomotopy charge
              in unstable
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+Borsuk"} Borsuk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Spanier"} Spanier
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+sets"} Cohomotopy sets
            %ul
              %li#Pontryagin38a
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Classification+of+continuous+maps+of+a+complex+into+a+sphere"} Classification of continuous maps of a complex into a sphere
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Communication I
              %li#Pontryagin50
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontryagin"}> Lev Pontryagin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+classification+of+mappings+of+an+%28n%2B2%29-dimensional+sphere+on+an+n-dimensional+one"} Homotopy classification of mappings of an (n+2)-dimensional sphere on an n-dimensional one
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/pont3.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              (both available in English translation in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "Revaz+Gamkrelidze#Gamkrelidze86"} Gamkrelidze 86
            %p as presented more comprehensively in:
            %ul
              %li#Pontryagin55
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth+manifolds+and+their+applications+in+Homotopy+theory"} Smooth manifolds and their applications in Homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/9789812772107_0001"} doi:10.1142/9789812772107_0001
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/pont001.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
              must have been known to Pontrjagin at least by 1936, when he announced the computation of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} second stem of homotopy groups of spheres
            %ul
              %li#Pontrjagin36
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
                ,
                %em Sur les transformations des sphères en sphères
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PontrjaginSurLesTransformationDesSpheres.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ) in:
                %em Comptes Rendus du Congrès International des Mathématiques – Oslo 1936
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathunion.org/fileadmin/ICM/Proceedings/ICM1936.2/ICM1936.2.ocr.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li#FreedUhlenbeck91
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
